/* app86: LE & CD Decoder — how to read a Loan Estimate and a Closing Disclosure, line by line, visually.
   1) Annotated Loan Estimate (3 pages) and Closing Disclosure (5 pages) laid out like the real H-24 / H-25 forms; every line is
      clickable: what it is, who is paid, shoppable?, TRID tolerance bucket, counts in the APR finance charge?, typical range, red flags.
   2) Cost encyclopedia: every fee type, filterable by loan program.
   3) Origination vs. discount points: what is allowed in each, QM points-and-fees and HOEPA limits, program rules
      (Conventional, FHA, VA, USDA, Jumbo/Non-QM, HECM, Texas 50(a)(6)) with a points-and-fees calculator.
   4) Concessions: interested-party contribution limits by program with a calculator.
   5) Decoder: enter the numbers from any LE / fee worksheet → math check, ratios, red flags, plain-English explanation;
      two anonymized samples from real documents preloaded; side-by-side compare.
   6) Tolerance checker: LE vs. CD by bucket → cure owed.
   Figures are summaries of 12 CFR 1026 (TRID, QM, HOEPA), HUD 4000.1, VA Pamphlet 26-7 / 38 CFR 36.4313, Fannie/Freddie guides,
   USDA HB-1-3555 and HUD HECM rules as Steven's team uses them; dollar thresholds adjust every year — verify current figures with
   the guide, the investor and the AE before advising. Not legal advice. */
const LD_TOL={zero:["0% tolerance","#dc2626","Can't increase from the LE at all (unless a valid changed circumstance and a revised LE). Any increase is cured with a refund."],ten:["10% aggregate","#d97706","All fees in this bucket together can rise up to 10% over the LE total; anything above 10% is cured."],none:["No limit","#16a34a","Can change in good faith — based on the best information at the time."],na:["n/a","#64748b","Not a fee — a total, credit or calculation."]};
